{"kind":"report","text":"Planner decision for 739aac5e (the package URI spelling), beside the pack output described in notes/implementation/2026-10-18-trusted-packages-developer.md at 03c93eb1.\n\nConfirmed: git+https://\u003chost\u003e/\u003crepository\u003e.git/@\u003ccommit\u003e/\u003cpath\u003e, with the constraints you list. The commit is the full lowercase hex id, 40 or 64 characters, and its length selects the object format the fetch must use. No credentials, query, fragment, empty or dot segments, and no floating ref of any kind. The host is lowercase, the repository spelling ends in .git with no trailing slash, and the path is the canonical percent-encoded tree path of the package file, relative to the tree root. Resolution removes git+ and the /@commit/path suffix to get the HTTPS remote, fetches only that commit, and reads only that path as a regular blob: a symlink, a submodule or an out-of-grammar path is refused without a fallback, the byte bound applies before parse, and there is no \"latest\".\n\nThe URI is assigned after the package file is committed, so it is outside the file it names and outside the manifest's digests; no self-reference.\n\nTrust is not the URI. The install act carries the URI and the expected release id as two separate fields, and the host admits the install only when that release id and the publisher key are on the operator's trust list and the fetched bytes produce that release id. The applications note's sketch \"dap app install \u003curi\u003e@\u003cid\u003e\" is a sketch; the command takes the URI and the release id as two arguments (for example a --release option), because the URI itself contains an @. Update the note's sketch when the install half lands, not before.\n\nKeep the retained fixture as you describe it: the real lending declaration, a labelled static page and a public test seed; not a converted, trusted, published or installed release. Keep the two retained failures in the note as failures.","body":{"request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:739aac5e9a907f0f99ba1682fe83592dd36574e4","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}